# Drop a sanitised telcoflo dump here (e.g. seed.sql / seed.sql.gz) to have it
# imported automatically the FIRST time the mysql container initialises an empty
# data directory. Files run in alphabetical order. Keep real dumps OUT of git.
#
# Example:
#   mysqldump -h 127.0.0.1 -uroot telcoflo | gzip > docker/mysql/initdb/seed.sql.gz
#   docker compose up -d          # imported on first boot
#
# After the File 03 converter has run once, set RUN_UPGRADE_BUILDERS=false so it
# is not re-run on every boot (it is idempotent, but skipping is cleaner).
